# 008 — an inventory item belongs to the seller of the offer that declared it.
#
# `createOffersWorkflow` linked every inventory item in a batch to
# `input.offers[0]?.seller_id ?? ""`, so one mixed-seller batch hands the whole
# batch to the first offer's seller (and an empty batch would link to seller
# `""`). The per-offer mapping already exists in the file as `offerSpans`; it is
# now used to build `(seller_id, inventory_item_id)` pairs in a `transform`.
#
# `linkSellerInventoryItemStep` takes those pairs instead of one `seller_id`, so
# its compensation dismisses exactly the rows it created. Its second caller,
# `createSellerInventoryItemsWorkflow`, is updated in the same patch and keeps
# its single-seller behaviour. A missing `seller_id` now throws instead of
# silently linking to the empty string.

